<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Weißenburg in Bayern</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Weissenburg in Bavaria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Weißenburg in Bayern is a town in Middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, beside the Roman fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biriciana">Biriciana</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raetian-limes">Raetian Limes</a>. It was a free imperial city from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> until 1802, long rivalled by the margraves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-ansbach">Brandenburg-Ansbach</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wulzburg">Wülzburg</a> fortress above it, and passed to Bavaria in 1802–1803.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/weissenburg-in-bayern.jpg" alt="Weißenburg in Bayern" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: wuppertaler · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GER_Wei%C3%9Fenburg_in_Bayern,_Altes_Rathaus_0010.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
